    "Kia-only Australian new-vehicle reconciliation as of 14 October 2026. Scope includes passenger BEVs and people movers; no new commercial-van research or lower-tier additions. Two independent Kia-brand model lists are explicitly narrower than the whole Australian Tier1 market, so publishedLists/listResolutions are intentionally empty and global C1 is not claimed.",
    "Current Australian factory/configurator family list is EV3, EV4 Sedan, EV5, EV6 and EV9. Exact current grades and body identities have been checked against maker Australian model pages, configurators and brochures. Distinct residual model years remain separate.",
    "EV3 GT-Line AWD is now present in the official current MY27 configuration flow; inherited provisional wording is removed based on current offering evidence. EV4 current maker list remains a FWD sedan with three grades; hatch, AWD and GT announcements overseas do not establish an Australian current exact offering.",
    "EV9 GT is a six-seat MY26 vehicle in the current four-grade Australian configurator. The linked brochure footer says As of 12 February 2027, which is after this review. That dating conflict is preserved; current order advertising is assessed separately. A seven-seats-up cargo heading is not silently assigned to the six-seat GT.",
    "Niro is absent from current maker navigation/build selection and CarExpert labels it discontinued, while CarsGuide still includes it in the current range. Only freshly verified exact authorised-dealer New residual versions are admitted, with stock advertised rather than physically verified. S and GT-Line historical grade existence alone does not prove current new supply.",
    "PV5 Passenger is reported for Q4 2026 and has regulatory approval, but current official Australian electric range and Build and Price expose PV5 Cargo only. No current exact Australian passenger-grade retail offer/order acceptance is established; no overseas specification or unannounced price is imported.",
    "EV2 is not in the current Australian maker electric range or Build and Price. Australian reporting quotes Kia saying import is highly unlikely because of European production cost/logistics. CarsGuide’s older-model accordion entry is not current Australian sale evidence.",
    "PV5 Cargo and future PV7 are commercial vehicles outside this pass. Petrol/hybrid Carnival, Cerato, K4, Picanto, Seltos, Sorento, Sportage, Stonic and Tasman entries are outside the BEV scope. No commercial data has been newly researched or changed.",
    "Inherited Kia Tier1 audit records are EV4, EV6 and EV9, with no Kia unverifiedLeads. EV3/EV5 were already catalogued; no invented audit rows are created.",
    "The inherited EV6 residual audit is checked at its finite original URLs: two exact MY26 Air RWD and GT-Line RWD New advertisements remain listed separately from the current MY27 model. Previously rejected demo, sold, conflicting and unavailable pages retain explicit dispositions in the family reconciliation; none establishes extra current residual supply."
